"Earnings Withholding Order | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/WG-002)\nciteturn1994search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Earnings Withholding Order (WG-002)\n\n# Earnings Withholding Order (WG-002)\n\nTells the employer (orders) to garnish wages of an employee. This sheriff, marshal, or constable may prepare this form or ask you to prepare it for them.\n\nGet form WG-002\n\n  * 汉语Get form WG-002 in Chinese Simplified (Chinese Simplified)\n  * 한국어Get form WG-002 in Korean (Korean)\n  * españolGet form WG-002 in Spanish (Spanish)\n  * Tiếng ViệtGet form WG-002 in Vietnamese (Vietnamese)\n\nEffective: January 1, 2026\n\n  * Go to How-to instructions for Debt Collection--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=rules-court%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1994search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; | WG-002 S | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order (Spanish) |  |\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS\n\n| Form number | Effective date | Form title | [Rev. January 1, 2026] |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| WG-002 S | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order (Spanish) |  |\n| WG-002 V | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order (Vietnamese) |  |\n| WG-003* | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) |  |\n| WG-003 C | 9/1/2023 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Chinese) |  |\n| WG-003 K | 9/1/2023 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Korean) |  |\n| WG-003 S | 9/1/2023 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Spanish) |  |\n| WG-003 V | 9/1/2023 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Vietnamese) |  |\n| WG-004* | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order For Support |  |\n| WG-004 C | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order For Support (Chinese) |  |\n| WG-004 K | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order For Support (Korean) |  |\n| WG-004 S | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order For Support (Spanish) |  |\n| WG-004 V | 2/22/2025 | Earnings Withholding Order For Support (Vietnamese) |  |\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWG-002\n\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY:  \nNAME (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rules-20230405-materials.pdf)\nciteturn1994search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; WG-002 ... EARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDER ... A judgment creditor has obtained this order to collect a court judgment against your employee. ... www.courts.ca.gov\nWG-002\n\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY:  \nNAME:  \nFIRM NAME:  \nSTREET ADDRESS:  \nCITY:  \nSTATE:  \nZIP CODE:  \nTELEPHONE NO.:  \nFAX NO.:  \nEMAIL ADDRESS:  \nATTORNEY FOR (name):  \nSTATE BAR NO.:\n\nLEVYING OFFICER (Name and address):\n\nDRAFT\n\n3/15/2023\n\nNOT APPROVED BY THE JUDICIAL COUNCIL\n\nSUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF  \nSTREET ADDRESS:  \nMAILING ADDRESS:  \nCITY:  \nZIP CODE:  \nBRANCH NAME:\n\nPLAINTIFF/PETITIONER:  \nDEFENDANT/RESPONDENT:\n\nEARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDER  \n(Wage Garnishment)\n\nLEVYING OFFICER FILE NO.:  \nCOURT CASE NO.:\n\nEMPLOYEE: KEEP YOUR COPY OF THIS LEGAL PAPER.  EMPLEADO: GUARDE ESTE PAPEL OFICIAL.\n\nEMPLOYER: Enter the following date to assist your recordkeeping.  \nDate this order was received by employer (specify the date of personal delivery by levying officer or registered process server or the date mail receipt was signed):\n\nTO THE EMPLOYER REGARDING YOUR EMPLOYEE:\n\nName and address of employer\n\nName and address of employee\n\nSocial Security No. ☐ on form WG-035 ☐ unknown\n\n1. A judgment creditor has obtained this order to collect a court judgment against your employee. Do not withhold more than the total of these amounts. Never withhold any earnings payable before the beginning of the earnings withholding period.\n\n3. The judgment was entered in the court on (date):  \nThe judgment creditor (if different from the plaintiff) is (name):\n\n4. The INSTRUCTIONS TO EMPLOYER on the reverse tell you how much of the employee's earnings to withhold each payday and answer other questions you may have.\n\nDate:\n\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME)                                                                                                                             (SIGNATURE)\n\n☐ LEVYING OFFICER     ☐ REGISTERED PROCESS SERVER\n\n(Employer's Instructions on reverse)\n\nPage 1 of 2\n\nForm Adopted for Mandatory Use  \nJudicial Council of California  \nWG-002 [Rev. September 1, 2023]\n\nEARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDER  \n(Wage Garnishment)\n\nCode of Civil Procedure, §§ 706.022, 706.108, 706.125  \nwww.courts.ca.gov\n\n3--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJudicial Council of California . Administrative Office of the Courts (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/itema4.pdf)\nciteturn1994search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 15.1 years ago; Crawled: 6 months ago; WG-002 ... The Employer's Return (form WG-005) describes several situations that could affect the withholding period for this order. ... IT IS ILLEGAL TO AVOID AN EARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDER BY POSTPONING OR ADVANCING THE PAYMENT OF EARNINGS.\nINSTRUCTIONS TO EMPLOYER ON EARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDERS  \nWG-002\n\nThe instructions in paragraph 1 on the reverse of this form describe your early duties to provide information to your employee and the levying officer.\n\nYour duties are TO WITHHOLD THE CORRECT AMOUNT OF EARNINGS (if any) and PAY IT TO THE LEVYING OFFICER during the withholding period.\n\nThe withholding period is the period covered by the Earnings Withholding Order (this order). The withholding period begins ten (10) calendar days after you receive the order and continues until the total amount due, plus additional amounts for costs and interest (which will be listed in a levying officer's notice), is withheld.\n\nIt may end sooner if (1) you receive a written notice signed by the levying officer specifying an earlier termination date, or (2) an order of higher priority (explained on the reverse of the EMPLOYER'S RETURN) is received.\n\nYou are entitled to rely on and must obey all written notices signed by the levying officer.\n\nThe Employer's Return (form WG-005) describes several situations that could affect the withholding period for this order. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nI N V I T A T I O N T O C O M M E N T (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/itc/w26-02.pdf)\nciteturn1994search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; WG-002 ... If you receive more than one *Earnings Withholding Order* during a withholding period, review form WG-005 for instructions. ... This calculation is summarized in the next section of this form and on the California Courts self-help website (selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/guide-earnings-withholding-orders-employers).\nINSTRUCTIONS TO EMPLOYER ON EARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDERS  \nWG-002\n\nThe instructions in paragraph 1 on page 1 of this form describe your initial duties to provide information to your employee and the levying officer.\n\nYour other duties are TO WITHHOLD THE CORRECT AMOUNT OF EARNINGS (if any) and PAY IT TO THE LEVYING OFFICER during the withholding period.\n\nThe withholding period is the period covered by *Earnings Withholding Order* (this order). The withholding period begins 30 calendar days after **you were served** with the order and continues until you have withheld the total amount due, plus additional amounts for costs and interest (which will be listed in a levying officer's notice). However, if the employee files a claim of exemption and notifies you of the filing no later than 29 days after **you were served** with *Earnings Withholding Order*, then the withholding period begins 45 days after **you were served** with *Earnings Withholding Order*.\n\nThe withholding period may end sooner if (1) you receive a written notice signed by the levying officer specifying an earlier termination date, or (2) you receive an order of higher priority (explained on page 2 of Employer's Return (form WG-005)).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=rules-court%2Fappendix_0.pdf)\nciteturn1994search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; WG-002* | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS\n\nForm number | Effective date | Form title | [Rev. July 21, 2026]\n---|---|---|---\nVL-120 | 9/1/2018 | Application for Order to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List |\nVL-125 | 9/1/2018 | Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List |\n\nWage Garnishment\n\nForm number | Effective date | Form title\n---|---|---\nWG-001* | 1/1/2012 | Application For Earnings Withholding Order\nWG-002* | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order\nWG-002 C | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Chinese)\nWG-002 K | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Korean)\nWG-002 S | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Spanish)\nWG-002 V | 1/1/2026 | Earnings Withholding Order (Vietnamese)\nWG-003* | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment)\nWG-003 C | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Chinese)\nWG-003 K | 1/1/2026 | Employee Instructions (Wage Garnishment) (Korean)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRules Committee E-Binder_April_10_2025 (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rules-20250410-materials.pdf)\nciteturn1994search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; WG-002 ... EARNINGS WITHHOLDING ORDER ... A judgment creditor has obtained this order to collect a court judgment against your employee. ... courts.ca.gov\nWG-002\n\nATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY:  \nNAME:  \nFIRM NAME:  \nSTREET ADDRESS:  \nCITY:  \nTELEPHONE